spans.s:
Keśarin,
(1) in LV 〔170.16〕, or Kesari-rāja, RP 〔22.16〕, n. of a king, former incarnation of Śākyamuni, alluded to in these vss.; his story is unknown to me;
(2) kesarin, n. of a battle-array (saṃgrāma; so also in Pali, n. of a saṃgāma): Av 〔i.56.4〕;
(3) Keśarin, n. of a former Buddha: Sukh 〔6.13〕.
